model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "An MCP session keeps ranked tool-search pages only under a key holding the request's complete ranking input (targets with their account sets, labels, scopes from the request's live policy, grant and tool availability, below, terms, offset and limit) and each target's listing version (digest and evaluation time), which every search reads by primary key before ranking; a page is kept only when the ranking statement read the same versions in its own snapshot. The memo never decides access: authentication, grant and policy checks and discovery still run on every request. Each session keeps at most 16 pages, none over 128 KiB and 512 KiB in all, measured as UTF-16 JSON, drops pages older than five minutes whenever it is read or written, and hands out copies. Outside an MCP session nothing is kept. The pages live only in the session object's memory, unlike its protocol sessions and request records, which its storage keeps, so an eviction drops them and the next search ranks afresh."
    }
  }
}
